:"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/status/triaged","name":"status/triaged","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Triaged and routed (see agent note)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":38,"created_at":"2026-11-05T05:03:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T05:32:41Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T05:32:37Z","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"status":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Part of the worlds design program: [#5955](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5955). Statements S24–S27 of the 2026-11-04 brief.\n\n## Requirement (Drew, in substance)\n\nOur side of the bargain is narrow, and it is the whole safety story:\n\n- **Ticks, sessions, or gas stay below a certain amount.** Budgets are platform-enforced, not author-promised.\n- **The platform side is solid — it can't be exploited to do more than it's meant to.** The capability ceiling is a security boundary, not a convention.\n- **Users are aware of what could be done.** Awareness (registry listing, permission prompts) is a load-bearing part of the model, not decoration.\n- Within those bounds — disk size and the rest — **users can pull whatever libraries they want**. No additional gatekeeping is implied by this design.\n\n## Design points to settle\n\n- The budget vocabulary: per-tick gas, per-session totals, per-world aggregate, disk quota per world / per user / per library cache. Which are hard kills, which are throttles, which are bills (see the compile-economics child of [#5955](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5955))?\n- Observability: what does a world author / server admin see when a budget trips — and what does the *user whose function tripped it* see? (The brief's program framing names observability as a first-class axis.)\n- Exploit-resistance review surface: enumerate the platform functions as an attack surface; for each, what bounds it (path sandboxing, network egress rules, allocation limits). This is the checklist the \"can't be exploited\" claim will be audited against.\n- Failure containment: a world that blows its budget must not degrade co-resident worlds on the same server.\n\n## Related\n\n- Per-function gas/timeout research child of [#5955](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5955)\n- Writer-set authority (adjacent boundary): [#5545](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5545)\n- Sandbox implementation today: `pkgs/id/src/sandbox.rs`; capability catalog `pkgs/id/crates/id-core/src/world_caps.rs`\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA design doc: the budget set with enforcement semantics, the observability surface for each budget, and the platform attack-surface checklist.\n","closed_by":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/5962/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/